<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAFRICA TOLL ROAD TARIFFS TO RISE 7.25 PCT MARCH 1.</title>
<headline>SAFRICA TOLL ROAD TARIFFS TO RISE 7.25 PCT MARCH 1.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South African Ministry of Transport announced on Monday that it would increase toll road tariffs by an average 7.25 percent with effect from March 1 in line with the rise in consumer inflation.</p>
<p>It said the increases stemmed from debt incurred to finance, operate and maintain toll roads.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
